    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d251">

                <pb facs="0444" n="410" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg410"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 252.</note>
                <head>Mr. Fish to Mr.
                        Thornton.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-04-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 21, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 14th instant, inclosing a copy of a dispatch from his
                    excellency the Governor General of the Dominion of Canada, and of the papers
                    which accompanied it. I must invite your attention and that of her Majesty’s
                    authorities to the first paragraph of the order in council of the 8th of January
                    last, as quoted in the memorandum of the Prime Minister of the Dominion of
                    Canada, accompanying the dispatch of his excellency <pb facs="0445" n="411"
                        xml:id="pg411"/> the Governor General, which paragraph is in the following
                    language, to wit:</p>
                <p>That the system of granting fishing license to foreign vessels, under the act 31
                    Vic., cap. 61, he discontinued, <hi rendition="#italic">and that henceforth all
                        foreign fishermen be prevented from fishing in the waters of
                    Canada.</hi></p>
                <p>The words underscored seem to contemplate an interference with rights guaranteed
                    to the United States under the first article of the treaty of 1818, which
                    secures to American fishermen the right of fishing in certain waters which are
                    understood to be claimed at present as belonging to Canada.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
